{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 7.468,
   "text": "The cellar in my rental house has thirteen wooden steps."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.068,
   "end": 16.495,
   "text": "The landlord taped one rule to the cellar door. Count the steps every time. If you ever count fourteen... go back up. And don't look down."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 17.295,
   "end": 20.495,
   "text": "I laughed at it. Old house. Old man."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.595,
   "end": 27.504,
   "text": "But I counted anyway, every night, going down for firewood. Thirteen. Always thirteen."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 28.304,
   "end": 29.968,
   "text": "Until last night."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.368,
   "end": 35.099,
   "text": "Eleven... twelve... thirteen..."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 36.299,
   "end": 39.499,
   "text": "And my foot came down on one more step."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 40.899,
   "end": 45.677,
   "text": "It wasn't wood. It was soft... and warm. And very slowly... it breathed."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 46.877,
   "end": 52.787,
   "text": "I didn't look down. I backed up those stairs, counting every one out loud, and slammed the door."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.787,
   "end": 58.755,
   "text": "Then I called the landlord. He was quiet for a long time."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 59.755,
   "end": 63.125,
   "text": "Then he asked, How many did you count going back up?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 64.325,
   "end": 66.608,
   "text": "I told him. Fourteen."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 68.208,
   "end": 71.579,
   "text": "He said, Then it isn't in the cellar anymore."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 73.779,
   "end": 79.475,
   "text": "The line went dead... and under my chair, the kitchen floor took one slow, warm breath."
  }
 ],
